{"product_id":"wish-list","title":"Wish List","description":"\u003cp\u003eInspire your students' creative writing with this witty story of good and evilMeg Finn is in a sticky situation. Killed in a gas explosion after a botched robbery attempt, Meg's soul is up for grabs. Heaven and Hell try every trick in the book to claim it, but Meg has a choice - helping a lonely old man complete tasks on his wish list will help her case with St Peter. But will she take it? Age 11+Bisto Merit Award WinnerRich in imagination and characterisation. This is an ideal model for students' own creative writing.Click here to read an EXTRACTClick here to download FREE TEACHING RESOURCES for The Wish ListTo automatically receive all the latest news on New Windmills, why not sign-up for our Heinemann Literature e-newsletter?\u003cbr\u003e\nDimensions: 132 x 194\u003cbr\u003e\nAuthor: Eoin Colfer\u003cbr\u003e\nISBN: 9780435130558\u003cbr\u003e\nFormat: Hardcover\u003cbr\u003e\nPages: 179\u003c\/p\u003e","brand":"bookhero.ae","offers":[{"title":"Default Title","offer_id":45404979691673,"sku":"17RE-3-9780435130558","price":5.0,"currency_code":"AED","in_stock":true}],"thumbnail_url":"\/\/cdn.shopify.com\/s\/files\/1\/0580\/5696\/6297\/files\/6829938d0e50d-Wish-List-Eoin-Colfer-_1.jpg?v=1752084415","url":"https:\/\/bookhero.ae\/products\/wish-list","provider":"Dubai - Buy Used\/Second-Hand Books - BookHero","version":"1.0","type":"link"}